body: "PR #42 introduces a custom-provider regression: `cite` accepts `././sample.txt`, but `affected({changed:['././sample.txt']})` silently skips that citation using the identical operand. The report says `complete: true` and `sourceComplete: true` without reading the changed source. The same built-package reproduction returns the affected row immediately before #42.\n\nVerified on `049dc82bdb0edfa259ffd6c8454cd9104d4b3f29` and its parent `2c538630acd8be8d24a0c2537daf400f1ffef717`, with Node 24.19.0 and lockfile dependencies. The adapter is a deterministic in-process fixture; no source file, service, or model is involved.\n\n### Exact source\n\n- [Custom-provider normalization removes exactly one leading `./`, so it is not idempotent](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-evidence/blob/049dc82bdb0edfa259ffd6c8454cd9104d4b3f29/src/sources.ts#L8-L17).\n- [Citation creation stores the result of one normalization](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-evidence/blob/049dc82bdb0edfa259ffd6c8454cd9104d4b3f29/src/evidence.ts#L11-L19).\n- [The new filter normalizes both the raw operand and the already-normalized stored source](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-evidence/blob/049dc82bdb0edfa259ffd6c8454cd9104d4b3f29/src/evidence.ts#L105-L117).\n\nFor this input, the stored source is `./sample.txt`. At filtering time, the raw operand becomes `./sample.txt`, while the stored source becomes `sample.txt`. They cannot match, so the source is skipped before verification.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n```sh\nreview=$(mktemp -d)\ngit clone --quiet https://github.com/unbraind/pm-evidence.git \"$review/package\"\ncd \"$review/package\"\ngit checkout --quiet 049dc82bdb0edfa259ffd6c8454cd9104d4b3f29\nnpm ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund\nnpm run build\ncat > repro-custom-path.mjs <<'JS'\nimport { mkdtemp } from 'node:fs/promises';\nimport {tmpdir} from 'node:os';\nimport {join} from 'node:path';\nimport {PmClient} from '@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk';\nimport {cite,check,affected} from './dist/index.js';\nimport {digest} from './dist/src/core.js';\nconst root=await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(),'evidence-repro-'));const workspace=join(root,'tracker');\nconst client=new PmClient({cwd:root,pmRoot:workspace,author:'fixture',noExtensions:true});\nawait client.init('sample',{defaults:true,agentGuidance:'skip',mergeFence:false});\nconst item=(await client.create({title:'Opaque source',type:'Task'})).item.id;\nlet changed=false;const calls=[];const adapters=[{provider:'opaque',read:async source=>{calls.push(source);const text=source+(changed?':new':':old');return{text,revision:digest(text)};}}];\nconst opts={workspace,root,author:'fixture',adapters,budget:10000};\nawait cite(item,'././sample.txt',{...opts,provider:'opaque',selector:{kind:'lines',start:1,end:1}});\nchanged=true;\nconst all=await check([],{...opts,record:false});\nconst filtered=await affected({...opts,changed:['././sample.txt']});\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify({check_rows:all.rows.length,check_freshness:all.rows[0]?.freshness,filtered_rows:filtered.rows.length,source_complete:filtered.receipt.sourceComplete,complete:filtered.receipt.complete,filtered_reads:filtered.receipt.verification.sourceReads,calls}));\nJS\nPM_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1 PM_AGENT_PROBES=0 NODE_ENV=test node repro-custom-path.mjs\n```\n\nObserved on #42:\n\n```json\n{\"check_rows\":1,\"check_freshness\":\"changed\",\"filtered_rows\":0,\"source_complete\":true,\"complete\":true,\"filtered_reads\":0,\"calls\":[\"sample.txt\",\"sample.txt\"]}\n```\n\nRun the exact same fixture against the parent:\n\n```sh\ngit checkout --quiet 2c538630acd8be8d24a0c2537daf400f1ffef717\nnpm run build\nPM_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1 PM_AGENT_PROBES=0 NODE_ENV=test node repro-custom-path.mjs\n```\n\nObserved before #42:\n\n```json\n{\"check_rows\":1,\"check_freshness\":\"changed\",\"filtered_rows\":1,\"source_complete\":true,\"complete\":true,\"filtered_reads\":1,\"calls\":[\"sample.txt\",\"sample.txt\",\"sample.txt\"]}\n```\n\n### Expected versus actual\n\nExpected: a filter using the identical accepted source operand finds the changed citation. Alternatively, unsupported identities must refuse explicitly before citation creation; an accepted source must not disappear behind an affirmative completeness receipt.\n\nActual: the unfiltered check reports the citation as changed, but filtered impact analysis returns zero rows, performs zero source reads, and reports complete/source-complete success. This worked before the merged normalization change.\n\n### Impact and suggested direction\n\nChanged-source-driven review can miss custom-provider evidence and its dependent tasks after the upgrade. The new filesystem normalization tests pass, including the custom-provider repeated-separator case; they do not cover repeated leading `./` with the same creation/filter operand.\n\nMake provider identity handling consistent across raw operands, stored descriptors and adapter/cache reads. Either use an idempotent provider-specific canonicalization or distinguish raw and already-normalized identities so a stored custom identity is not stripped again. Preserve opaque custom identifiers and legacy citations rather than applying filesystem normalization indiscriminately. Add a before/after regression for this exact-input property.\n\nDuplicate check: all-state searches for `custom provider path`, `canonical affected`, `opaque`, and `custom normalization`, plus the full issue inventory. Closed [#40](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-evidence/issues/40) concerns equivalent **filesystem** spellings and explicitly asks to preserve arbitrary custom-provider identities. This report is the newly introduced **custom-provider** regression in its fix; the parent control succeeds. No duplicate of #40 is being asserted for the fixed filesystem case."
